WAVE 4 GOAL:
Make KB Admin consume the centralized authorization model consistently for Knowledge Base access, hierarchy nodes, workflows, and content types.

SCOPE:

1. KB ADMIN AUTHORIZATION
Integrate KB Admin with the centralized permission evaluator.

Authorization must support:
- Knowledge Base
- Hierarchy node
- Workflow
- Content type

Use the existing centralized evaluator and existing ALLOW/DENY + scope semantics from Wave 3.

2. ROLES / GROUPS / USERS
Update KB Admin permission management so administrators can:
- View permissions for users/groups/roles
- Assign permissions
- Remove permissions
- Distinguish inherited permissions from explicit permissions
- Show the source of the effective permission

Do not introduce a parallel authorization model.

3. EFFECTIVE PERMISSIONS
Provide/use APIs for:
- Effective permissions
- Permission sources
- Explicit permissions
- Inherited permissions
- Permission inheritance through the hierarchy

The UI must clearly distinguish:
- Explicit permission
- Inherited permission
- Effective permission
- Permission source

4. OVERRIDES
Support the existing centralized permission model for:
- Creating permission overrides
- Removing permission overrides
- Viewing current overrides

Respect the existing hierarchy inheritance behavior.

5. API PROTECTION
Protect KB Admin APIs using the same centralized evaluator.

Do not rely only on frontend hiding/disabling.
Every protected backend operation must enforce authorization server-side.

6. HIERARCHY INHERITANCE
Ensure permissions inherited from parent hierarchy nodes are correctly reflected on child nodes.

Do not duplicate permission calculations in the frontend.

7. FRONTEND
Update the KB Admin UI to consume the centralized authorization APIs.

Keep the existing UI design unless a change is required for authorization clarity.

The UI should clearly show:
- Effective permission
- Permission source
- Explicit vs inherited
- User/group/role
- Scope
